message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on mouth tape. Knit fabric with adhesive, in pre-cut shapes. The candidates are 5906 (rubberized textile fabrics) or 3919 (self-adhesive plates, sheets, tapes), but 3919 covers plastics only. Textile fabric coated with adhesive in strips up to 20 cm wide falls under 5906.10 (adhesive tape of a width not exceeding 20 cm). Heading 5906: "Rubberized textile fabrics, other than those of heading 5902"; 5906.10.00 is "Adhesive tape of a width not exceeding 20 cm". Another option is 5806 or 5603, but adhesive-coated fabric goes to 5906. Chapter 30 (3005, wadding, gauze, bandages and similar articles coated with adhesive for medical, surgical, dental or veterinary purposes) is not applicable because this is not a medical use. Mouth tape for sleeping is therefore not medical, and 5906.10.0000 is the likely result.

The HTSUS 5906.10.00 subheading is a single line, 5906.10.0000.

{"hts_code": "5906.10.0000", "reason": "Knit textile fabric coated with acrylate adhesive, imported as pre-cut tape strips under 20 cm wide, is classified as adhesive tape of textile fabric in heading 5906, subheading 5906.10."}
